# Potato Soup

Based on [https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1024500-potato-soup](https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1024500-potato-soup) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20260112181248/https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1024500-potato-soup))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 6 slices [bacon]{ ing="bacon" } (about 10 ounces), diced into 1/2-inch pieces
- [ ] 2 Tbsps [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }
- [ ] 3 [celery stalks]{ ing="celery-stalks" }, finely chopped
- [ ] 1 large [yellow onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, finely chopped
- [ ] 1 large [carrot]{ ing="carrot" }, peeled and finely chopped
- [ ] 2 [garlic cloves]{ ing="garlic-cloves" }, finely chopped
- [ ] [Kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } (such as Diamond Crystal) and black pepper
- [ ] 3 pounds [Yukon gold potatoes]{ ing="yukon-gold-potatoes" } (about 6 medium), peeled and diced into 1-inch cubes
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [chopped fresh thyme]{ ing="chopped-fresh-thyme" }, or 1/4 tsp dried
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [ancho chile powder]{ ing="ancho-chile-powder" }, optional
- [ ] 4 cups [chicken broth]{ ing="chicken-broth" }
- [ ] 1/2 to 1 [cup heavy cream]{ ing="cup-heavy-cream" }, to taste
- [ ] [Shredded cheddar cheese]{ ing="shredded-cheddar-cheese" }, for serving
- [ ] [Finely chopped chives]{ ing="finely-chopped-chives" }, for serving

## Recipe

1. Heat a large Dutch oven or pot over medium heat. Add the [bacon]{ ing="bacon" } and cook, stirring occasionally, until crisp, 12 to 14 minutes. Transfer the bacon to a plate with a slotted spoon; set aside to use later as a topping.
1. Leave 1 Tbsp of the [bacon]{ ing="bacon" } fat in the pot. Over medium heat, add the [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }. Once melted, stir in the celery, [onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, [carrot]{ ing="carrot" } and garlic; season with a little [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and cook, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables have softened, about 10 minutes.
1. Stir in the [potatoes]{ ing="yukon-gold-potatoes" } and season well with [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and pepper. Sprinkle on the [thyme]{ ing="chopped-fresh-thyme" }, [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" } and [chile powder]{ ing="ancho-chile-powder" } (if using). Cook, stirring, for 2 minutes. Add the [broth]{ ing="chicken-broth" }, increase the heat to high and bring to a boil. Cover, reduce heat to medium-low and simmer, stirring occasionally, until the potatoes are fork tender, 15 to 20 minutes. As the soup simmers, taste the broth and add salt if needed. Stir in as much [heavy cream]{ ing="cup-heavy-cream" } as you like and remove from the heat.
1. Transfer half of the soup to a blender and process until smooth. Return the blended soup to the pot and cook on medium-low, uncovered and stirring occasionally, until the soup thickens slightly, about 15 minutes. (Alternatively, you can use an immersion blender and blend about half the soup in the pot.) Add more [heavy cream]{ ing="cup-heavy-cream" }, [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and pepper, if desired, and serve in bowls topped with [bacon]{ ing="bacon" }, [cheese]{ ing="shredded-cheddar-cheese" } and [chives]{ ing="finely-chopped-chives" }.

## Notes

- Luxurious, warm and filling, this classic soup checks all of the comfort food boxes. As the creamy Yukon gold potatoes cook, they release starches and thicken the broth. Half of the soup is blended for a contrast of textures, while the smoked paprika adds warmth, complementing the flavors of the bacon. Use as much cream as you like, but don’t be shy with it - it’s a welcome companion that doesn’t weigh down the soup, but rather lightens it. To serve, set up a toppings bar as you would for baked potatoes.
- Use an immersion blender (we have one) and consider bacon alternatives
